			<div class="content" id="post-content-2821278">
									

<p>-1 from me, I'm afraid.</p>
<p>As Accelerando mentioned, there's no actual description. Worse, it just continuously blurts the whole story out, one beat after another. It really doesn't fit clinical tone or the SCP format, but more importantly, it just isn't that interesting to read.</p>
<p>I think the real world references also took me out of it, but they probably wouldn't have been as bad if they weren't in the long litany of &quot;and then this happened and then this happened and then this happened&#8230;&quot;</p>
<p>You've gotta have some structure to your story. Everything the Foundation does here falls, but it fails pretty much the sentence after you mention it and then you plow right on, so it never comes as a twist or builds tension. (The &quot;comedic&quot; tone of the Foundation documents really did not help that.) All they ever discover is that it's more and more powerful. There's no hint to motive beyond&#8230; altruism maybe?</p>

