			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3627279">
									

<p>I agree, no vote one way or the other though. Despite the flawed structure, it is still an interesting scp, and I appreciate hat it isn't an openly hostile or threatening scp. The real world references definitely need revisement or censoring (whichever would work, i have no practice in writing), and a less story based structure, unless you intend to add an after incident report.</p>
<p>On the plus side the scp itself is interesting, and a nice break from the monsters and brain melting abominations to reality. It works in a creepy factor as well, and subtly. Altruism, without any kind of compensation, is suspicious to people, it is widely believed that strangers don't do public works unless they want something. And the tagline at the end about it being only the beginning helps.</p>
<p>In short, good premise, subtle threat, but poor structure and pacing. Needs a solid buildup to ending threat.</p>

